ArcticDownloader 0.2.4 update log

Purpose:
- Track code changes made in the Linux workspace so they can be mirrored in the Windows workspace.

Format:
- Date
- Change summary
- Files changed
- Notes

Entries:
- 2026-04-18
  - Fixed Linux folder picker integration so the app uses the GTK XDG Desktop Portal backend instead of falling back to Zenity when choosing ComfyUI folders.
  - Files changed:
    - src-tauri/src/main.rs
    - src-tauri/dist/main.js
    - src-tauri/Cargo.lock
    - packaging/arch/PKGBUILD
    - packaging/aur-bin/PKGBUILD
    - packaging/debian/debian/control
    - packaging/fedora/arctic-comfyui-helper.spec
    - CHANGELOG_0.2.4.md
    - version0.2.4_updates
  - Notes:
    - `pick_folder` now accepts an optional title, and the frontend passes contextual titles for the ComfyUI root, install base, workflow root, and shared models root pickers.
    - Direct `rfd` GTK backend testing was reverted because it could crash inside the Tauri/WebKit GTK runtime.
    - Native Linux packages now declare `xdg-desktop-portal-gtk` as a runtime dependency so fresh installs get the desktop-native GTK-style picker instead of the Zenity fallback.
- 2026-04-16
  - Updated workflow catalog handling so workflow rows can open external links instead of always downloading JSON files.
  - Files changed:
    - src/model.rs
    - src-tauri/dist/main.js
    - CHANGELOG_0.2.3.md
    - version0.2.3_updates
  - Notes:
    - Workflow catalog entries can now include optional `patreon_url`, `workflow_url`, or `workflow_link_url` fields.
    - `workflow_json_url` is now serde-defaulted so link-only workflow entries can load without a JSON download URL.
    - The workflow button label changes to `Open Workflow Link` for link-style entries and opens the URL through the existing external browser command.
    - Workflow dropdown labels now prefer full-name fields such as `workflow_name`, `name`, or `title` before falling back to `display_name`.
- 2026-04-15
  - Reworked the Models tab hardware sizing logic from broad range labels to fixed standard hardware-size mappings.
  - Files changed:
    - src-tauri/dist/main.js
    - src/vram.rs
    - src/ram.rs
    - Cargo.toml
    - Cargo.lock
    - src-tauri/Cargo.toml
    - src-tauri/Cargo.lock
    - src-tauri/tauri.conf.json
    - packaging/arch/PKGBUILD
    - packaging/debian/debian/changelog
    - packaging/fedora/arctic-comfyui-helper.spec
    - CHANGELOG_0.2.3.md
    - version0.2.3_updates
  - Notes:
    - The hardware-size mappings match common fixed GPU VRAM and system RAM capacities.
    - Removed the redundant `32+ GB VRAM` option from the fixed GPU VRAM mapping so 32 GB is represented once.
    - The fixed-size values are mapped back to the existing internal catalog tiers so the current catalog schema remains compatible.
    - The AUR binary package files should be updated with `scripts/update-aur-bin.sh --version 0.2.3` after the 0.2.3 Arch release artifact exists, so the checksum can be generated from the real package.
- 2026-04-15
  - Hid the Models tab GPU VRAM and RAM dropdowns and switched model guidance to automatic hardware detection.
  - Files changed:
    - src-tauri/dist/index.html
    - src-tauri/dist/main.js
    - src-tauri/dist/styles.css
    - CHANGELOG_0.2.3.md
    - version0.2.3_updates
  - Notes:
    - RAM guidance now uses the detected system RAM tier.
    - GPU VRAM guidance uses the detected NVIDIA VRAM size when available.
    - NVIDIA VRAM guidance now uses nominal MiB bands so 32 GB cards that report slightly under 32 GiB still map to the 32+ GB VRAM tier.
    - If GPU VRAM size cannot be detected, the app still shows all manual variants without blocking downloads.
- 2026-04-15
  - Changed model variant selection to be manual instead of VRAM-filtered.
  - Files changed:
    - src-tauri/dist/main.js
    - src/ram.rs
    - CHANGELOG_0.2.3.md
    - version0.2.3_updates
  - Notes:
    - The Models tab now shows all variants for the selected model family, with detected GPU VRAM used only to sort variants and warn when a variant may need more VRAM than detected.
    - Model search now includes variant IDs, model sizes, quantization labels, and notes so users can find variants such as `3B Q8`.
    - Model downloads no longer require choosing GPU VRAM or RAM first.
    - RAM `min_ram_tier` checks now behave as minimum requirements, so a stronger RAM tier includes artifacts marked for weaker RAM tiers.
- 2026-04-15
  - Added exact RAM bucket support for alternative artifacts.
  - Files changed:
    - src/model.rs
    - src-tauri/dist/main.js
    - CHANGELOG_0.2.3.md
    - version0.2.3_updates
  - Notes:
    - Artifacts can now use `ram_bucket` for exact RAM-bucket selection, which is intended for alternatives such as Q5/Q4/Q3 text encoders.
    - `min_ram_tier` remains supported separately as a true minimum requirement.
- 2026-04-15
  - Added queue checkboxes for selectable model support files.
  - Files changed:
    - src-tauri/dist/main.js
    - src-tauri/dist/styles.css
    - src-tauri/src/main.rs
    - CHANGELOG_0.2.3.md
    - version0.2.3_updates
  - Notes:
    - RAM-bucketed support files are now all shown in the Selected Queue, but only the detected best RAM bucket is checked by default.
    - Optional LoRAs, upscalers, and other support files are checked by default and can be unchecked before download.
    - The selected checkbox set is passed to the backend so unchecked files are not downloaded.
- 2026-04-15
  - Replaced raw model family IDs with friendly family labels in the Models tab UI.
  - Files changed:
    - src-tauri/dist/main.js
    - CHANGELOG_0.2.3.md
    - version0.2.3_updates
  - Notes:
    - The model family dropdown still stores the catalog `family` ID internally, but users see labels derived from model display names, such as `LTX 2.3` or `FLUX 1`.
- 2026-04-15
  - Prioritized Clip and Text Encoder groups in the Selected Queue.
  - Files changed:
    - src-tauri/dist/main.js
    - CHANGELOG_0.2.3.md
    - version0.2.3_updates
  - Notes:
    - The catalog order is unchanged; the app only sorts the queue display so Clip/Text Encoder support files appear above optional extras.
- 2026-04-15
  - Made Models tab search global only when no model family is selected.
  - Files changed:
    - src-tauri/dist/main.js
    - CHANGELOG_0.2.3.md
    - version0.2.3_updates
  - Notes:
    - With an empty search box, the model family dropdown still filters normally.
    - With no family selected, search text searches all model families.
    - With a family selected, search text searches only inside that family.
- 2026-04-15
  - Made model variant dropdown defaults follow the detected GPU VRAM recommendation.
  - Files changed:
    - src-tauri/dist/main.js
    - CHANGELOG_0.2.3.md
    - version0.2.3_updates
  - Notes:
    - Variant lists are ranked by detected GPU VRAM and preserve catalog order inside the same recommendation rank.
    - Checked models keep following the recommended variant unless the user manually changes that model's variant dropdown.
    - `Select Visible` now selects the recommended variant for each visible model.
